{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Components"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It keeps a copy of the graph to look vertices up through the graph’s own vertex indices, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"text":" hashes nothing on a graph whose indices are its vertices. The copy shares","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage (copy-on-write), so making it is O(1), and later changes to the original do not affect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the result. The cost comes later: while the result is alive, the next mutation of the original","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copies the whole graph, as it would with any other copy. Drop the result, or keep only what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you need from it (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array(components)"},{"text":"), before mutating the graph.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A component’s slice keeps the indices of the flat storage it is cut from, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CompressedSparseRow.successors(of:)"},{"text":" does: use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first"},{"text":", iteration or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array(_:)"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[0]"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because its type names the graph’s type, a result cannot be returned through an existential"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": call it from a generic function ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"some DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A partition of a graph’s vertices into components, in a documented order: a collection of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, each a slice of vertices in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, with an O(1) "},{"code":"component(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/endIndex","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/startIndex"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(checked:)","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(of:)","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(ofIndex:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Subscripts","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/subscript(_:)"],"anchor":"Subscripts"},{"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/Element","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/Index","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connecti